}}

==Enemy==
This dastardly duck has enormous health and attack power, and though his [[Multi-Hit]] works the same as that of [[Casaurian Ahirujo]] and [[Casaurian Darkjo|Darkjo]], those in the range of the last hit are damaged the most. Additionally, he has a 50% chance to spawn a Level 2 [[Surge Attack]] on his last hit that could appear anywhere up to 750 range. Combined with his immunities to [[Slow]], Surges, and worst of all, [[Knockback]], this enemy can ravage both your frontline ''and'' backline if not defeated fast enough.

==Strategy==
Magamojoe pushes even harder than his other variants, and his Relic trait makes him quite the handful, as few accessible units could counter Relic Behemoths, not to mention the presence of other support units that can block usual counters like [[Idi:N (Special Cat)|Idi:NX]] (although her Surge immunity allows her to sprint past and deal heavy damage just as Magamojoe's multi-hits conclude) and Surges wiping out your weaker units. It's also very difficult to regain ground against his Knockback and Slow immunities, so in many cases you would prefer luring him with better positioning. Having [[Elder Mask Doron (Special Cat)|Awakened Doron]], [[Elder Beast Naala (Special Cat)|Awakened Naala]], and [[Dogumaru (Special Cat)|Reborn Warrior Doguemon]] will definitely ease the fight, thanks to their anti-Relic/Behemoth abilities coming into play and allowing them to somewhat tank him.

