==Trivia==
*The name Magamojoe (マガモジョー ''Magamojō'') may be derived from 真鴨 ''magamo'' ([[wikipedia:Mallard|mallard duck]]), ''mojo'' (plural ''mojos'' or ''mojoes''; a magic spell or hex, referencing his Curse ability), イビルジョー ''Ibirujō'' (the Japanese name of ''Monster Hunter''<nowiki>'</nowiki>s [[wikia:monsterhunter:Deviljho|Deviljho]]) and ジョー ''jō'' (jaw, referring to his large beak). Like Magamojoe, both male mallard ducks and Deviljho have a prominent green coloration.
*His crest, beak shape, arms and feathers all resemble those of [[wikia:monsterhunter:Kulu-Ya-Ku|Kulu-Ya-Ku]], a Bird Wyvern introduced in ''Monster Hunter World''. Fittingly, Kulu-Ya-Ku is a very early-game monster, and Magamojoe debuts in the very first stage of [[Legend Stages# Zero Legends|Zero Legends]]. His lack of the "Casaurian" prefix from [[Casaurian Ahirujo]] and [[Casaurian Darkjo]]'s names may be because Kulu-Ya-Ku, unlike [[wikia:monsterhunter:Yian Garuga|Yian Garuga]], is not a close relative of [[wikia:monsterhunter:Yian Kut-Ku|Yian Kut-Ku]].
*His Japanese description is a reference to the [[wikipedia:Star of the Giants|''Star of the Giants'']] character [[wikia:kyojin-no-hoshi:Ittetsu Hoshi|Ittetsu Hoshi]], who also looks after three children, has a cruel and unorthodox style of education, and is very infamous for a [[wikia:kyojin-no-hoshi:Iconic Kyojin no Hoshi scenes that are mostly parodied#Chabudai Gaeshi|scene]] where he slapped his son [[wikia:kyojin-no-hoshi:Hyūma Hoshi|Hyūma]] and knocked over the dinner table at the same time.
*He and [[Ultima Beast Naala]] are the only Behemoths to share the same title in their Japanese names. Both are titled ''Chō Kojū'' (超古獣, "Super Ancient Beast").
*It can be assumed that Ancient Magamojoe's three children are the three Bird Brothers mentioned in [[Casaurian Darkjo]]'s description.
*Although Casaurian Ahirujo, Casaurian Darkjo and Ancient Magamojoe all have ジョー ''jō'' in their Japanese names, it was romanized inconsistently in English: "jo" for the Casaurians, "joe" for Magamojoe.

